# PRD and Plan Documents

When writing or editing PRDs and plan documents (e.g. in `PRD/` or similar):

1. **Prefer numbered lists over bullet lists** for any list of requirements, steps, options, scope items, goals, or open points. This makes it easier to refer to specific items in conversation (e.g. "implement step 3", "what about item 5?").
2. Use a single numbering style per section (1. 2. 3. …). Sub-items can use nested numbers (1.1, 1.2) or letters (a, b) when needed.
3. Implementation outlines, scope (in/out), goals, dependencies, open points, and references should use numbered lists unless the content is a single paragraph or a table.
4. **Structure:** New PRDs should follow the **one-folder-per-PRD** structure (see `PRD/prd-template.md`): `PRD/<short-title>/` with `prd.md`, `agent-actions.md`, and optional `e2e/`. Use **PRD Generator** (`.cursor/commands/prd-generator.md`) to scaffold; validate with **Review PRD before agent** (`.cursor/commands/review-prd-before-agent.md`).
